cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  shmap-rs: a Rust port of shmap, with a reproducible
  cross-architecture benchmark suite
message: >-
  If you use this software or its benchmark result sets,
  please cite it using the metadata below. The algorithm is
  Ivanov et al.'s; please cite the original shmap as well.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Panchev
    given-names: Dobromir
    email: dobromir.panchev@gmail.com
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0000-2636-2593'
  - family-names: Ivanov
    given-names: Pesho
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8119-3849'
repository-code: https://github.com/d0bromir/shmap-rs
license: MPL-2.0
version: 1.6.0
date-released: 2026-09-13
abstract: >-
  A Rust port of shmap, a sketch-based long-read mapper that
  locates a read by k-mer set overlap rather than by
  alignment. The default mapper preserves the original
  algorithm, with threading and memory optimizations.
  Opt-in adaptive mapping adds positional sampling,
  persistent indexing, batching, and native repeat rescue.

  The repository also carries the evidence: a versioned
  benchmark suite and separate native-only adaptive
  experiments on x86_64 and aarch64. The latter preserve
  240 measurements with matching normalized output across
  hosts, documenting both deep-HiFi gains and dense-index
  and ONT regressions. Adaptive MAPQ is unavailable, and
  no tenfold improvement or general accuracy claim follows.
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - sequence alignment
  - long-read mapping
  - minimizers
  - sketching
  - reproducible benchmarking
  - rust
references:
